  "instruction": "For each supplied membership episode expiring in calendar 2025, return episode_id INTEGER and covered BOOLEAN ordered by episode_id ascending. One confirmed renewal for that member must begin at or before expiry and end at or after expiry plus 14 elapsed 24-hour days. These endpoint comparisons are inclusive even though no activity interval union is computed. Multiple adjacent renewals cannot be stitched. All renewal years participate; other statuses do not. An episode is the supplied unique episode_id, not the member's first purchase; multiple episodes per member are independently tested and one renewal may cover multiple episodes. No renewal gives FALSE. Renewal rows are arbitrary bags: repeated and conflicting intervals are separate evidence and existence prevents multiplication. Empty episodes produce no rows. All times are naive, timezone-free, microsecond-resolution timestamps; no calendar-date cast or rounding. All input columns are nonnull, episodes.episode_id must be unique and every renewal ends_at must be >= begins_at. No other uniqueness, foreign-key or status-enum restriction; orphan renewals are ignored. No tie selection or NULL ordering is applicable.",
